1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,420
The Cold War explained, like you are five.

2
00:00:02,420 --> 00:00:05,160
Step one, in 1945, the war ends,

3
00:00:05,160 --> 00:00:06,380
and the two countries that won it

4
00:00:06,380 --> 00:00:08,260
are already suspicious of each other.

5
00:00:08,260 --> 00:00:10,600
American soldiers and Soviet soldiers shake hands

6
00:00:10,600 --> 00:00:12,200
in the middle of a ruined Germany,

7
00:00:12,200 --> 00:00:14,180
and then they draw a line and stop.

8
00:00:14,180 --> 00:00:15,520
The Americans have something new.

9
00:00:15,520 --> 00:00:18,240
In August, they dropped two atomic bombs on Japan,

10
00:00:18,240 --> 00:00:20,960
and the war in the Pacific ends in nine days.

11
00:00:20,960 --> 00:00:24,440
For four years, only one country on Earth has that weapon.

12
00:00:24,440 --> 00:00:27,160
They did not become enemies because of what they believed.

13
00:00:27,160 --> 00:00:28,960
They became enemies because one of them

14
00:00:29,000 --> 00:00:30,240
was holding something.

15
00:00:30,240 --> 00:00:33,400
In 1949, the Soviets test one of their own.

16
00:00:33,400 --> 00:00:35,480
Step two, now both of them have it,

17
00:00:35,480 --> 00:00:36,860
and both of them keep building.

18
00:00:36,860 --> 00:00:40,100
By the 1980s, there are more than 60,000 nuclear weapons

19
00:00:40,100 --> 00:00:42,160
in the world, and that creates a strange rule.

20
00:00:42,160 --> 00:00:44,200
If either one attacks, both of them die.

21
00:00:44,200 --> 00:00:46,800
So the two most heavily armed countries in history

22
00:00:46,800 --> 00:00:49,560
never fight each other, not once, not one battle.

23
00:00:49,560 --> 00:00:51,240
Instead, they fight everywhere else

24
00:00:51,240 --> 00:00:52,520
through other people's countries

25
00:00:52,520 --> 00:00:53,920
with other people's soldiers.

26
00:00:53,920 --> 00:00:56,760
Korea, Vietnam, Angola, Afghanistan.

27
00:00:56,760 --> 00:00:59,080
The weapon that made the two of them safe from each other

28
00:00:59,080 --> 00:01:00,920
made everybody else the battlefield,

29
00:01:00,920 --> 00:01:03,000
and in one city, the line runs straight down

30
00:01:03,000 --> 00:01:04,360
the middle of the street.

31
00:01:04,360 --> 00:01:06,720
Step three, Germany is split in two,

32
00:01:06,720 --> 00:01:08,880
and Berlin sits deep inside the Soviet half

33
00:01:08,880 --> 00:01:10,760
and is itself split in two.

34
00:01:10,760 --> 00:01:12,680
For years, people simply walk across,

35
00:01:12,680 --> 00:01:15,400
and the ones who walk west mostly do not come back.

36
00:01:15,400 --> 00:01:17,640
Doctors, engineers, teenagers.

37
00:01:17,640 --> 00:01:20,440
So on the night of the 13th of August, 1961,

38
00:01:20,440 --> 00:01:22,760
without warning, soldiers roll out barbed wire

39
00:01:22,760 --> 00:01:24,840
across the streets while the city is asleep.

40
00:01:24,840 --> 00:01:27,320
People wake up on the wrong side of their own city.

41
00:01:27,320 --> 00:01:28,600
The wire becomes a wall.

42
00:01:28,600 --> 00:01:29,800
The wall gets a second wall

43
00:01:29,800 --> 00:01:31,240
and a strip of sand between them

44
00:01:31,240 --> 00:01:32,960
where anyone crossing can be seen.

45
00:01:32,960 --> 00:01:34,680
It was not built to keep an enemy out.

46
00:01:34,680 --> 00:01:36,320
It was built to keep its own people in.

47
00:01:36,320 --> 00:01:39,200
For 28 years, that wall is the safest place in the war

48
00:01:39,200 --> 00:01:40,240
because the dangerous part

49
00:01:40,240 --> 00:01:42,320
is happening somewhere nobody can see.

50
00:01:42,320 --> 00:01:44,800
Step four, October, 1962.

51
00:01:44,800 --> 00:01:46,560
The Soviets put nuclear missiles in Cuba,

52
00:01:46,560 --> 00:01:49,280
and for 13 days, the world sits closer to the end

53
00:01:49,280 --> 00:01:50,240
than it ever has.

54
00:01:50,240 --> 00:01:52,640
That one gets solved by two men making a deal.

55
00:01:52,640 --> 00:01:54,040
The others get solved by luck.

56
00:01:54,040 --> 00:01:56,360
On the 26th of September, 1983,

57
00:01:56,360 --> 00:01:57,840
a Soviet early warning system

58
00:01:57,840 --> 00:02:00,080
reports five American missiles incoming.

59
00:02:00,080 --> 00:02:01,400
The officer on duty that night

60
00:02:01,400 --> 00:02:03,680
is supposed to pick up the phone and report an attack.

61
00:02:03,680 --> 00:02:05,160
He decides the computer is wrong

62
00:02:05,160 --> 00:02:07,120
and reports a malfunction instead.

63
00:02:07,120 --> 00:02:07,960
He is right.

64
00:02:07,960 --> 00:02:10,680
Everybody was afraid of a machine deciding to end the world.

65
00:02:10,680 --> 00:02:13,080
It nearly ended because a machine was believed.

66
00:02:13,080 --> 00:02:14,680
The war does not end in a battle.

67
00:02:14,680 --> 00:02:16,360
It ends in an accounting office.

68
00:02:16,360 --> 00:02:18,520
Step five, the Soviet Union is spending

69
00:02:18,520 --> 00:02:21,360
enormous amounts of money on weapons, on Afghanistan,

70
00:02:21,360 --> 00:02:23,100
and on holding half of Europe.

71
00:02:23,100 --> 00:02:26,100
Then the price of oil collapses, and oil is what it sells.

72
00:02:26,100 --> 00:02:27,140
It is running out of money,

73
00:02:27,140 --> 00:02:29,740
and the countries it controls start pulling away.

74
00:02:29,740 --> 00:02:31,860
On the 9th of November, 1989,

75
00:02:31,860 --> 00:02:33,780
an East German official is handed a note

76
00:02:33,780 --> 00:02:35,380
about relaxing the travel rules

77
00:02:35,380 --> 00:02:37,060
and reads it out at a press conference

78
00:02:37,060 --> 00:02:38,460
without reading it first.

79
00:02:38,460 --> 00:02:40,660
A journalist asks when this takes effect.

80
00:02:40,660 --> 00:02:43,140
He looks at the paper and says, immediately.

81
00:02:43,140 --> 00:02:45,860
Within hours, thousands of people are standing at the wall

82
00:02:45,860 --> 00:02:47,460
and the guards, with no orders,

83
00:02:47,460 --> 00:02:49,820
and nobody answering the phone, open it.

84
00:02:49,820 --> 00:02:52,740
For 40 years, two countries pointed 60,000 warheads

85
00:02:53,260 --> 00:02:54,620
and never fired one.

86
00:02:54,620 --> 00:02:56,180
The thing that finally opened the border

87
00:02:56,180 --> 00:02:58,220
was a man who did not read his notes.

88
00:02:58,220 --> 00:03:00,700
And that's just one story inside Paladin.

89
00:03:00,700 --> 00:03:02,940
It's like Duolingo, but for history lovers,

90
00:03:02,940 --> 00:03:05,420
download it now and become the most intelligent person

91
00:03:05,420 --> 00:03:06,260
in the room.

